title: Goodryke Unveils His Cabinet
subtitle: The "Cabinet of Lords", they call it.
view-if: chancellor = "Goodryke" and papen_time == 1
on-arrival: chancellor_party = "I"; finance_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; economic_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; justice_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; foreign_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; army_minister = "I"
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/papen_cabinet.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The Cabinet of Lords

Ferris Goodryke has unveiled his new cabinet—assembled almost entirely on Staal’s recommendations. The Forward wasted no time branding it the “Cabinet of Lords,” with six members drawn from the nobility and only three being commoners. The overtly anti-social character of the cabinet has already alienated the vast majority of the country and firmly sealed Goodryke’s vast unpopularity among the Commonwealth people.

The only party formally represented in the cabinet is the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, which holds three ministries. The remaining posts are occupied by right-wing independents, in line with Goodryke’s stated goal of forming a government "free from party influence." Staal has been promoted to Defense Minister, where he intends to steer the administration from behind the scenes.

At present, only Mallin’s [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?] are prepared to back the cabinet when the Assembly reconvenes.

- @papen

@papen
title: Goodryke announces his goals to the nation.
on-arrival: commons_marcher += 2; commons_collectivist += 2; pro_republic -= 3

In his first radio address to the Commonwealth people, Goodryke laid out the ideological direction of his government. He denounced previous administrations for steering the Commonwealth toward "<span style='color: #9B0000;'>state Reformism</span>," blaming them for the "moral decay" wrought by an "unholy class war" and "cultural <span style='color: #9B0000;'>radical Collectivism</span>." He also condemned the transformation of the Commonwealth into a welfare state and seeks to reverse our progress over the years.

As The Forward puts it, this marks "a unique declaration of class war from above." The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>—and even more so the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>—after months of decline, are poised for resurgence as the battle between the barons and the people begins. Moreover, if the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> were to back this cabinet, it could trigger a collapse in their popular support.

- @papen_2

@papen_2
title: The Assembly is dissolved for new elections.
subtitle: As part of Staal's promise to [+ royalist_leader +].
view-if: next_election_time >= time+1
on-arrival: next_election_time = time+1 if next_election_time >= time+1; next_election_month = month + 1 if next_election_time >= time+1; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+1; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_week = week + 7; next_election_week -= 4 if next_election_week > 4; next_election_week -= 4 if next_election_week > 4; next_election_week = 4 if next_election_week == 0

Goodryke has dissolved the Assembly to spark new elections, as apart of their promise to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and the hope that they'll win the most seats in the Assembly, allowing Goodryke a majority needed to establish an authoritarian government.

New Assembly elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +], Week [+ next_election_week +].